"SpacetimeDB Identity corresponds to a specific client connection/device, so trust must not attach to identities directly. Add an accounts layer between identities and everything that means anything durable (roles, player components): (1) accounts table -- the durable principal; (2) account_identities relation mapping one account to one or more connection identities; (3) login machinery: an unattached identity requests login to an account, creating a PENDING login-request row that is subscribed/visible to all of the account's already-attached identities (visibility guaranteed -- the request cannot be hidden), and one of those existing identities must explicitly confirm (or deny) before the new identity is attached; (4) account creation bootstraps the first identity; (5) roles reference ACCOUNTS, not identities (reshapes the admin-auth task: claim_admin_role grants the role to the calling identity's account); (6) player ownership (player_controller_components.identity, new_player, reconnect/deactivation grace) resolves identity -> account at the connection boundary so all gameplay state hangs off the account. The confirmation flow is the security model: even leaked credentials cannot silently attach a device, because attachment is always visible to and gated by existing devices. Fail fast per project rule: unattached identities attempting privileged/owned actions get errors, not fallbacks. Precedes admin-auth-via-a-published-secret-token."